From a68db7ad8af375d4d831193bcee0f62d9a5a2f90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:21:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Pool attestation judges only eligible members: one
 held worker no longer makes access-label cards home-only

kanban-1663abf6ab (t_01a1cef258d944e9): attested() returned False when ANY pool
member was held, inactive, pickup-off or stale. On 11-12 worker-1 was held, so
every hub card whose text derived a coordination label (token-broker,
kanban_show, hermes-hub status) got portable_reason "needs worker coordination
capability", no worker-first-v1 enrollment, and waited up to 37 h for a full
hub while workers 2-6 carried every label.

- kanban_placement_coordination.eligible(): active, unheld, pickup, fresh
  (<=300 s) members; a missing registry entry is skipped (the Board leases it
  nothing), a non-dict entry fails closed. attested() is True only when at
  least one eligible member remains and every eligible member carries the
  labels. The claim gate still rechecks the actual destination.
- Declared access (requires ssh:mbp / ssh:mini / hub:read) stays home-only
  with portable_reason "declared access the Board cannot place": hermes-hub
  worker_placement.ts supportedRequirement places only terminal/file/git/
  kanban/hub:write, so an enrolled card would queue for good
  (task_requirement_unsupported). BOARD_PLACEABLE_ACCESS = {hub:write} (the
  one main's ACCESS_LABELS adds that the Board maps) is the mirror to widen;
  the check runs after structural_reason(). (PR #1330 review 5872124183.)
- Board reserve: unchanged. worker_placement.ts selects from the whole
  configured pool through available(), which already skips held/inactive/
  pickup-off/stale machines (request candidates are only an allowlist check);
  hermes-hub worker-placement.test.ts covers held -> queued.
- Detection: a ready local-lane card created with that reason now reads
  "Home-only by a stale creation verdict ...: pool worker(s) X now carry its
  access labels and have free slots. Re-place it (hermes kanban move <card>
  ...)" in queue / queue_note (coordination.stranded re-runs the full
  portable_reason against just those workers, so other home markers still pin).

Tests: test_kanban_coordination_placement.py (new cases fail on main);
declared-access contract tests run with the Board mapping simulated.
